{"title":"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 23","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Algebraic_approach_via_Sum-to-Product_Identity)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Algebraic approach via Sum-to-Product Identity)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The solutions of the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/c/a2cb3321c19030e888eb1ca227f8a810113ff81a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^4+4z^3i-6z^2-4zi-i=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"229\" height=\"18\" /> are the vertices of a convex polygon in the complex plane. What is the area of the polygon?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/3/e6385e906feb4d945a33951796c9e40e8a51a1da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)}\\ 2^{\\frac{5}{8}}\\qquad\\mathrm{(B)}\\ 2^{\\frac{3}{4}}\\qquad\\mathrm{(C)}\\ 2\\qquad\\mathrm{(D)}\\ 2^{\\frac{5}{4}}\\qquad\\mathrm{(E)}\\ 2^{\\frac{3}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"382\" height=\"22\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Looking at the coefficients, we are immediately reminded of the binomial expansion of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/f/49f95e0041b1dec5c1142ae57607e277aae7e2db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${\\left(x+1\\right)}^{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>Modifying this slightly, we can write the given equation as:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/0/e10a3fa3d0bae693db18fc3ac2f6ac67bbf43a78.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[{\\left(z+i\\right)}^{4}=1+i=2^{\\frac{1}{2}}\\cos \\frac {\\pi}{4} + 2^{\\frac{1}{2}}i\\sin \\frac {\\pi}{4}\\]\" width=\"299\" height=\"33\" />\nWe can apply a translation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/d/0fda51aabf3fa68a72ba3b46518abc175c76dab2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-i$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> and a rotation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/5/3451d596b6a4f234ff34902d7af2947375ba4525.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\frac{\\pi}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"27\" height=\"33\" /> (both operations preserve area) to simplify the problem:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/9/769db790032db3f7a51b9f866767cb64a99aa2b7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[z^{4}=2^{\\frac{1}{2}}\\]\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Because the roots of this equation are created by rotating <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/e/aeebb746f8c0d3dac5219c3635617032430afee9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\pi}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"17\" height=\"34\" /> radians successively about the origin, the quadrilateral is a square.\n</p><p>We know that half the diagonal length of the square is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89f5a8001ddd97d63d230f7bb4602c595b139192.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${\\left(2^{\\frac{1}{2}}\\right)}^{\\frac{1}{4}}=2^{\\frac{1}{8}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"92\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, the area of the square is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/9/7e9dc1e144fdc1eec9ec4b39b69fa7e0e811acbb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{{\\left( 2 \\cdot 2^{\\frac{1}{8}}\\right)}^2}{2}=\\frac{2^{\\frac{9}{4}}}{2}=2^{\\frac{5}{4}} \\Rightarrow D.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"213\" height=\"55\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Algebraic_approach_via_Sum-to-Product_Identity.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Algebraic_approach_via_Sum-to-Product_Identity)\">Solution 2 (Algebraic approach via Sum-to-Product Identity)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Algebraic approach via Sum-to-Product Identity)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Observing the coefficients of the given equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/d/0fd3034ca4fb0d0892716971b70211b67bdbe857.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^4 + 4iz^3 - 6z^2 - 4iz - i = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"229\" height=\"18\" />, we notice its similarity to the binomial expansion of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/7/38763a87416ef6900e009eb1f9a5b5eb5df550fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(z+i)^4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"61\" height=\"21\" />. \nRecall that:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/3/a83cfe822196a1944a584c19f9f66ecd4ab21587.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(z+i)^4 = z^4 + 4iz^3 + 6(i)^2z^2 + 4(i)^3z + i^4 = z^4 + 4iz^3 - 6z^2 - 4iz + 1\\]\" width=\"537\" height=\"20\" />\nThus, the original equation can be rewritten as:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/2/802dbfa539b16a6a4185e8a5e6e3c09f4a2b8b01.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(z+i)^4 - 1 - i = 0 \\implies (z+i)^4 = 1+i\\]\" width=\"320\" height=\"20\" />\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/7/0474c933fbc5c48aadd69e64d3455fe5279b4752.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w = z+i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" />. In polar form, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/b/91b21e9181637fe3ff5d386074f24ea0410f7dd5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+i = \\sqrt{2} e^{i\\frac{\\pi}{4}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"113\" height=\"21\" />. The four roots for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee4b825a2e36ae093ed7be5e4851ef453b34914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> are given by:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/b/d8be5145367f1b8d271856a5b961b2c7e7448517.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[w_k = \\left(2^{\\frac{1}{2}}\\right)^{\\frac{1}{4}} e^{i\\left(\\frac{\\pi/4 + 2k\\pi}{4}\\right)} = 2^{\\frac{1}{8}} e^{i\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{16} + \\frac{k\\pi}{2}\\right)}, \\quad k \\in \\{0, 1, 2, 3\\}\\]\" width=\"427\" height=\"37\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/c/77c6624828589d036d3b7f162c25271f1b77e8fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_k = w_k - i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"92\" height=\"17\" />, the side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> of the square formed by these vertices is the distance between two adjacent roots, such as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/b/bab9abe98679312d2a3308c76188cf2cbc492f68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/a/9ea31e5c5613f025b5be8aca425d318168491d89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />. Note that the constant translation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/d/0fda51aabf3fa68a72ba3b46518abc175c76dab2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-i$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> cancels out when taking the difference:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/3/da31a2ce06ee0c090f9b58e80f3c922ef9f285bb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[s = |z_1 - z_0| = |w_1 - w_0| = 2^{\\frac{1}{8}} \\left| e^{i\\frac{9\\pi}{16}} - e^{i\\frac{\\pi}{16}} \\right|\\]\" width=\"332\" height=\"33\" />\nExpanding using Euler's formula <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/e/01e62fce9c87ab7c5cc62ed65793e98fe05c8d5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e^{i\\theta} = \\cos\\theta + i\\sin\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"149\" height=\"19\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/d/72d399116759a6218c2c6afbdabe5460968e55a1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[e^{i\\frac{9\\pi}{16}} - e^{i\\frac{\\pi}{16}} = \\left( \\cos\\frac{9\\pi}{16} - \\cos\\frac{\\pi}{16} \\right) + i \\left( \\sin\\frac{9\\pi}{16} - \\sin\\frac{\\pi}{16} \\right)\\]\" width=\"429\" height=\"43\" />\nApplying the sum-to-product identities:\n</p>\n<ul><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/8/4e8a9e82cad831e01a2317c4e1b8a3c6f5edf5d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos A - \\cos B = -2\\sin\\frac{A+B}{2}\\sin\\frac{A-B}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"320\" height=\"39\" /></li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/1/541cee0f9be2341136d5ee3d7a3c649a5b88a3fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin A - \\sin B = 2\\cos\\frac{A+B}{2}\\sin\\frac{A-B}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"304\" height=\"39\" /></li></ul>\n<p>Setting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/4/e247b112b4fab82a343199e479f2e15d58771318.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = \\frac{9\\pi}{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"64\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/6/686386c96e1443b4e9ddff90af1cf1b27321210b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B = \\frac{\\pi}{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"63\" height=\"34\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/2/d625adc146511219086360e7601b01197e750616.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{A+B}{2} = \\frac{5\\pi}{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"105\" height=\"39\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/9/7b972924b0727063f6d92a97b5c4cbca958c7bcd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{A-B}{2} = \\frac{\\pi}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"96\" height=\"39\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/4/fb4beeaa0bb5b3eeea1d9771e77e01f80ac24f77.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[e^{i\\frac{9\\pi}{16}} - e^{i\\frac{\\pi}{16}} = -2\\sin\\frac{5\\pi}{16}\\sin\\frac{\\pi}{4} + i \\left( 2\\cos\\frac{5\\pi}{16}\\sin\\frac{\\pi}{4} \\right) = 2\\sin\\frac{\\pi}{4} \\left( -\\sin\\frac{5\\pi}{16} + i\\cos\\frac{5\\pi}{16} \\right)\\]\" width=\"625\" height=\"43\" />\nThe magnitude of the term in the parentheses is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/3/f738f89ca1f65bceaed536ddeff1c750803f50ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{(-\\sin\\theta)^2 + (\\cos\\theta)^2} = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"206\" height=\"35\" />. Given <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/e/fcea0ea8dd5134d654fe9fb6d04498cfb327e8eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin\\frac{\\pi}{4} = 2^{-\\frac{1}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"96\" height=\"34\" />, the side length is:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/f/1efe8027ced7fa82a83ff33ef3558476fc32441b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[s = 2^{\\frac{1}{8}} \\cdot \\left| 2 \\cdot 2^{-\\frac{1}{2}} \\cdot 1 \\right| = 2^{\\frac{1}{8}} \\cdot 2^{\\frac{1}{2}} = 2^{\\frac{5}{8}}\\]\" width=\"269\" height=\"33\" />\nThe area of the square is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/2/752ccf51ef0be42644a0099346e876310df962f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"17\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/c/94c16f9a769a995ecd4562980807183488414c95.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\text{Area} = (2^{\\frac{5}{8}})^2 = 2^{\\frac{10}{8}} = 2^{\\frac{5}{4}}\\]\" width=\"190\" height=\"22\" />\nThe answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/d/87d32bac8c5abe4d6b299d444f24a8055279b232.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(D)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"24\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A\">2008 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 22\">Problem 22</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 24\">Problem 24</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017215031\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.042 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.062 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 292/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2298/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8351/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.382      1 -total\n 59.60%    7.976      1 Template:AMC12_box\n 37.80%    5.058      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:6475:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017215031 and revision id 278174. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}